Create a single-file HTML Google Reviews Sentiment Analyzer with no backend,
no build steps, and no external dependencies except Chart.js from CDN.

## Design
- Blue/purple gradient header: linear-gradient(135deg, #1d4ed8, #2563eb, #7c3aed)
- CSS custom properties for light and dark mode (toggle stored in localStorage)
- Colour-coded sentiment: green (positive), amber (neutral), red (negative)
- Smooth fade-in animations on results
- Responsive layout — stacks to single column on mobile

## Input Section
- Two-column layout: large textarea on the left, info/API panel on the right
- Textarea placeholder shows example reviews with instructions
- Reviews are separated by blank lines — one blank line = new review
- Three buttons: Analyze Sentiment, Load Sample Reviews, Clear
- Info panel explains how to copy reviews from Google Maps

## Optional Google Places API Integration
- Two input fields: Google Place ID and Google API Key (password field)
- "Fetch Reviews" button calls Google Places Details API
  URL: https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/place/details/json
       ?place_id={id}&fields=name,reviews&key={key}
- Extracts review text, joins with blank lines, auto-triggers analysis
- Handle CORS failure gracefully with a helpful error message
- Note: fetches up to 5 reviews per place

## Sentiment Analysis Engine (VADER-style, pure JavaScript)

### Lexicon
Build an AFINN-inspired lexicon of ~130 review-domain words scored -5 to +5:
- +5: excellent, outstanding, perfect, amazing, fantastic, phenomenal, flawless
- +4: great, awesome, best, love, terrific, fabulous, impressive, recommend
- +3: good, nice, happy, satisfied, friendly, helpful, delicious, professional
- +2: comfortable, convenient, affordable, beautiful, efficient, reliable, prompt
- +1: fair, decent, fine, okay, satisfactory, solid
- -1: average, mediocre, bland, forgettable, generic
- -2: disappointing, poor, overpriced, delayed, uncomfortable, underwhelming, stale
- -3: bad, rude, unprofessional, dirty, frustrating, broken, disgusting
- -4: terrible, awful, horrible, hate, worst, appalling, pathetic, abysmal
- -5: fraud, scam, ripoff

### Negation handling
Check a window of 3 words before each scored word.
Negation words: not, no, never, neither, cannot, can't, won't, don't, doesn't,
  didn't, isn't, aren't, wasn't, weren't, haven't, hasn't, hadn't, wouldn't,
  couldn't, shouldn't, without, barely, hardly, scarcely, lack, lacking
If a negation is found: multiply the word's score by -0.74 (partial flip)

### Intensifier scaling
Check a window of 2 words before each scored word.
Multipliers:
  ×1.5 — extremely, absolutely, utterly, exceptionally
  ×1.4 — completely, incredibly
  ×1.3 — very, super, seriously
  ×1.2 — really, definitely, truly, particularly, especially, deeply
  ×1.15 — so
  ×1.1 — quite, rather
  ×0.8 — fairly, almost
  ×0.7 — somewhat
  ×0.6 — slightly
  ×0.5 — barely

### Compound score formula (VADER normalisation)
compound = sum_of_scores / sqrt(sum_of_scores² + 15)
Result is always between -1.0 and +1.0, rounded to 2 decimal places.

### Classification thresholds
Positive: compound ≥ 0.05
Negative: compound ≤ -0.05
Neutral:  between -0.05 and 0.05

### Keyword extraction
Aggregate all lexicon words found across all reviews.
Separate into positive (score > 0) and negative (score < 0) lists.
Sort each list by total occurrence count, show top 12 per category.

## Results Section (shown after analysis, smooth scroll into view)

### Overall Sentiment — Score Ring + KPI Tiles
- Animated SVG circular ring gauge (radius 65, stroke 14)
  - Maps compound score (-1 to +1) onto the ring circumference
  - Ring colour: green (positive) / amber (neutral) / red (negative)
  - Centre text: compound score value + overall label (😊/😐/😞)
  - Animate ring fill on load using stroke-dashoffset transition
- 4 KPI tiles beside the ring:
  - Total Reviews (blue)
  - % Positive (green background)
  - % Neutral (amber background)  
  - % Negative (red background)

### Charts (Chart.js 4.4 from CDN)
- Doughnut chart: Positive / Neutral / Negative counts
  Colours: #16a34a / #d97706 / #dc2626
- Bar chart: individual compound score per review on x-axis (-1 to +1 y-axis)
  Bar colours match sentiment label, border-radius 5px

### Keywords
- Two side-by-side cards: Top Positive Keywords | Top Negative Keywords
- Each keyword shown as a colour-coded pill/tag with occurrence count
- Green pills for positive, red pills for negative

### Individual Review Cards
- Scrollable list (max-height 420px)
- Each card shows:
  - Truncated review text (180 chars max, ellipsis)
  - Sentiment badge (😊 Positive / 😐 Neutral / 😞 Negative)
  - Compound score number
  - Colour-coded progress bar (maps -1..+1 to 0..100%)
- Cards have hover border highlight

## Sample Data
Load 8 pre-written restaurant reviews covering a range of sentiments
(very positive, very negative, neutral, mixed) when "Load Sample Reviews" clicked.
Auto-trigger analysis after loading.

## Tech stack
- HTML5, CSS3 with custom properties
- Vanilla JavaScript ES6+ only
- Chart.js 4.4 via CDN (jsdelivr)
- No frameworks, no build tools, no npm
